=== S(t) as a driven QCA cell crosses its transition ===

  T =    1.0   S_max = 0.0000   at tau = 1.000   S_final = 0.0000
  T =    5.0   S_max = 0.0007   at tau = 0.914   S_final = 0.0005
  T =   20.0   S_max = 0.0025   at tau = 0.818   S_final = 0.0019
  T =  100.0   S_max = 0.0092   at tau = 0.725   S_final = 0.0051

Observation:
  S(t) peaks near the transition (tau ~ 0.5) and drops
  to zero after.  This is a transient entanglement burst.
  The peak grows with J/g and saturates at ln 2.

  Implication for QCA wires: at every clock edge a cell
  passes through an entangled regime.  If the clock is
  too fast, the cell cannot fully disentangle before the
  next operation -- residual entanglement becomes noise.
  This sets a QUANTUM SPEED LIMIT on QCA clock rate.
